# Monada Store — environment
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.env`
# 2. In Supabase: Project Settings → API
# 3. Paste the Project URL and the `anon` `public` key below
# 4. Run the SQL schema from the admin panel (Supabase & SQL tab)
# 5. Run: npm run verify:supabase
#
# The anon key is safe to ship in a browser bundle BY DESIGN — it is a public
# key. What protects your data is Row Level Security, not secrecy of this key.
# NEVER put the `service_role` key here: it bypasses RLS entirely and would
# hand full database control to anyone who views your site's source.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Optional: only used by `npm run verify:supabase`, never by the app.
#
# The catalog is world-readable, so the read checks need nothing more. Writing
# products, settings and photos requires a signed-in admin, so without these
# the write checks are reported as SKIPPED rather than failed. Set them to the
# Supabase Auth account you use for the admin panel to get a full report.
#
# These are deliberately not VITE_-prefixed, so Vite cannot bake the password
# into the browser bundle.
#
# VERIFY_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
# VERIFY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=your-admin-password
